.SH Overview
This tool generates a safety\-critical Hierarchical State Machine (HSM)
from a YAML/SMB definition file.
It supports four output languages \(em \f[B]Rust\f[R], \f[B]C\f[R],
\f[B]Python\f[R], and \f[B]TypeScript\f[R] \(em and includes advanced
features such as orthogonal regions (parallelism), history patterns,
decision trees, and fork transitions.
.PP
The generator also produces a \f[B]Graphviz DOT\f[R] file for
visualizing the state machine diagram.
.SH Obtaining and Installing
The source code is hosted on GitHub:
.PP
\f[CR]https://github.com/ingvast/SM\-code\-generator\f[R]
.PP
Clone the repository and follow the build and installation instructions
in the \f[CR]README.md\f[R] file in the repository root.
In short, the tool is packaged as a Python wheel and installed via
\f[CR]uv\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
uv build
uv tool install dist/smbuilder\-*.whl
.EE
.PP
After installation the \f[CR]sm\-compiler\f[R] command is available on
your \f[CR]PATH\f[R].
.SH Generating the Code
The \f[CR]sm\-compiler\f[R] command validates your model and produces
code in the selected target language.
.IP
.EX
\f[I]# Language is read from the \(aqlanguage:\(aq key in the .smb file\f[R]
sm\-compiler model.smb

\f[I]# Override the language\f[R]
sm\-compiler model.smb \-\-lang rust
sm\-compiler model.smb \-\-lang c
sm\-compiler model.smb \-\-lang typescript

\f[I]# Custom output base path (extensions added automatically)\f[R]
\f[I]# Produces build/myfsm.rs and build/myfsm.dot\f[R]
sm\-compiler model.smb \-o build/myfsm
.EE
