.SH SMB File Structure
The input file uses YAML syntax with the extension \f[CR].smb\f[R].
A complete model has this top\-level structure:
.IP
.EX
language\f[B]:\f[R] rust\f[I]              # Target language (rust, c, python, or typescript)\f[R]

includes\f[B]: \f[R]|\f[I]             # Code placed before the Context struct\f[R]
  // imports, helper functions, etc.

context\f[B]: \f[R]|\f[I]              # User\-defined fields for the Context struct\f[R]
  pub counter: i32,     # (Rust syntax)
  pub flag: bool,

context_init\f[B]: \f[R]|\f[I]         # Initialization code for context fields\f[R]
  counter: 0,           # (Rust: struct init syntax)
  flag: true,

hooks\f[B]:\f[R]\f[I]                  # Global code injected into all states\f[R]
  entry\f[B]: \f[R]|
    // runs on every state entry
  exit\f[B]: \f[R]|
    // runs on every state exit
  do\f[B]: \f[R]|
    // runs on every state tick
  transition\f[B]: \f[R]|
    // runs on every transition

initial\f[B]:\f[R] first_state\f[I]    # Name of the initial child state\f[R]

states\f[B]:\f[R]
  first_state\f[B]:\f[R]
\f[I]    # ... state definition ...\f[R]
.EE
