.SS Context Struct
All backends generate a \f[CR]Context\f[R] struct or class (Rust:
\f[CR]Context\f[R], C: \f[CR]SM_Context\f[R], Python/TypeScript:
\f[CR]Context\f[R]) containing:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]now\f[R]: Logical time (\f[CR]f64\f[R]/\f[CR]double\f[R]).
You update this before each tick.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]state_timers[]\f[R]: Per\-state entry timestamps (set
automatically on entry).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]transition_fired\f[R]: Safety flag for orthogonal regions (managed
automatically).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]terminated\f[R]: Set when a \f[CR]null\f[R] transition fires
(managed automatically).
.IP \(bu 2
Hierarchy pointers: Function pointers tracking the active state at each
level (managed automatically).
.IP \(bu 2
User fields: Whatever you declare in the \f[CR]context:\f[R] block.
.SH Writing Logic: Handlers vs. Hooks
.SS Local Handlers (Per State/Transition)
These are defined inside specific states or transitions in the YAML.
They apply only to that specific element.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]\f[CB]entry\f[B]\f[R]: Runs once when entering the specific state.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]\f[CB]do\f[B]\f[R]: Runs every tick while in the specific state.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]\f[CB]exit\f[B]\f[R]: Runs once when leaving the specific state.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]\f[CB]action\f[B]\f[R]: Runs during a specific transition (see
Section\ 7).
.SS Global Hooks (System\-wide)
Hooks are defined at the root level under the \f[CR]hooks:\f[R] key.
They inject code into \f[B]every\f[R] occurrence of an event type across
the entire machine (e.g., for logging).
